      ],
      "extract": "One of the most interesting open questions in theoretical physics is whether the unitary evolution of states in quantum theory is violated by gravitational eﬀects [1]. The debate has centered on the process of black hole formation and evaporation, where, at the semi- classical level, almost no information about the initial quantum state of the infalling matter appears to be carried by the ﬁnal outgoing Hawking",
