          "term": "event horizon",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "Before considering ﬁnite mass black holes it is instructive to consider the simpler geom- etry of Rindler space which can be viewed as the exterior region close to the horizon in the limit of inﬁnite black hole mass. It is also isomorphic to the region of ﬂat four-dimensional Minkowski space deﬁned by |z| > |t|, z > 0, shown in Figure 1. We introduce Rindler coordinates R, ω as follows, t = R sinh ω , z = R cosh ω .",
      "extractCut": true
    },
    {
