          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "gedanken experiments",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "The event horizon of Rindler space can be viewed as a black hole event horizon in the limit of inﬁnite mass. Any attempt by external observers to determine the physical presence of an information storing membrane outside a black hole event horizon will run into planckian obstacles just as in Rindler space. The discussion of the gedanken experiments of the previous section carries over to this case as the reader can",
      "extractCut": true
    },
