      ],
      "extract": "We wish to deﬁne a measure of the “lifetime” of information stored in a thermalized system, K, such as a black hole stretched horizon or a thermal cavity. Suppose at time t = 0, the system K is in some pure state ψ which is a typical member of a thermal ensemble with energy E and temperature T. Furthermore, let N(E) be the number of possible states at energy E. To begin with, the system has zero ﬁne grained entropy",
